cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SDRscan, please cite it as below, together with the tools it runs (findZX, BWA, freebayes, bcftools, bedtools, KMC, MUMmer)."
title: "SDRscan: identify sex chromosomes and the sex-determining region from whole-genome sequencing of males and females"
abstract: >-
  SDRscan is a pipeline to identify sex chromosomes and locate the
  sex-determining region (SDR) from whole-genome resequencing of males and
  females, for any ploidy. It combines read depth and heterozygosity (findZX
  and a ploidy-aware scan), sex-specific SNP density, sex-specific k-mers and
  assembly comparison, tests each candidate region (permutation tests, PCA,
  leave-one-out), distinguishes XY from ZW systems, and assigns genetic sex to
  samples of unknown sex.
authors:
  - family-names: Malik
    given-names: Hafiz Muhammad Talha
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/<user>/SDRscan"
